# Pages that are deliberately over the 8 KB ceiling, and why.
#
# The ceiling exists because every byte of a page is paid by the agent that opens
# it. A page is normally split when it exceeds the ceiling. These two are not,
# because splitting them would cost the reader more than the bytes do: each is
# opened to look one thing up, and the answer would land on the other side of the
# split as often as not.
#
# An exception is not free. A page listed here earns 70% of the credit a page
# within the ceiling earns, so the pressure to shrink it stays. An entry naming a
# page that does not exist, or one that is already under the ceiling, is a defect
# and is reported.
#
#   <page> = <bytes> # reason
#
22-state-machine.md = 11264  # one document format that cannot be half-learned: the transition rules and the operations table answer each other
51-debug.md         = 11264  # a symptom index; a split makes the reader guess which half their symptom is in. "Running the pieces" already came out of it as 50-running.md
